  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the goat as a stand-in for Muslims",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the goat, which is being used as a dehumanizing stand-in for Muslims in the meme. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the meme's structure and intent create an implicit projection where the viewer (user) is positioned as the one who 'got' the bootleg copy, thereby identifying with the act of acquiring the offensive content. The goat, as the central visual entity, becomes the projected entity onto which the user's identity is implicitly mapped in the context of the hate speech.",
